# 002-10 evidence (second set of runs, after review finding 1): ticklog lines of the mixer and the sender, the flood probe summaries, the acceptance counters and the derived statistics.
# Scratch copy: /home/dorian/workspace/hadronyche/poc-scratch at HEAD 2f29eba (002-07 hoplog) with the ticklog patch 002-10-scratch.diff applied for the runs and reverted afterwards; poc-untouched-equivalent otherwise.
# Three baseline/flooded run pairs, each run `hadropoc loopback --duration 30 --no-tui` on its own isolated group and port, 239.72.68.44:<group port>, --port <port>:
#   run 1: baseline group 44420 port 45500; flooded group 44421 port 45600
#   run 2: baseline group 44422 port 45700; flooded group 44423 port 45800
#   run 3: baseline group 44424 port 45900; flooded group 44425 port 46000
#   flooded runs: flood-send --target 127.0.0.1:<port+31> --rate 20000 --duration 28 --session <sender id> --ack-seq <sender id>
#   (the sender id is the one the ticklog prints at thread start, `ticklog module=sender id=<n>`; the flood starts 1.5 s after it)
# All 6 runs exit 0 (the status of each was checked; for the flooded runs via flooded*.sh, which prints `poc exit=0`) and the flood probe reports 0 send errors in each flooded run.
# Ticklog line fields: inN = datagrams received on input N in the 1 s window; inN_len = smallest..largest datagram length in bytes;
#   inN_audio = datagrams carrying an audio message; inN_ok = audio messages accepted by the mixer's `ok` length/format check (mixer.rs:93-98, poc-untouched);
#   inN_mixed = feed payloads for which audio::mix returned Some (summed); inN_echo_full / inN_echo_hdr = echoes sent with / without an audio message (len > HDR).
#   An absent counter means 0. *_cum_* figures are cumulative since the module's first datagram (1 us histogram buckets, exact max).


